{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A placeholder is often the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" thing on screen for a few hundred milliseconds, or the only thing a user with a slow connection sees for much longer than that — so it’s worth it being as accessible as the real content it stands in for. The default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefault{Empty,Loading,Error}View"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"type":"text","text":"s handle all of this out of the box; this article rounds up what they do and how a fully custom placeholder can match them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"VoiceOver announcements","type":"heading","anchor":"VoiceOver-announcements","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each default placeholder announces its own appearance — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_:).post()"},{"type":"text","text":" in SwiftUI, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.post(notification:.announcement, argument:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in UIKit — so a screen settling into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":" is heard, not just seen."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes that same wording for any case, so a fully custom placeholder can announce transitions consistently instead of inventing its own text:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onAppear {","    if let announcement = state.accessibilityAnnouncement {","        AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(announcement).post()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen. See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for the full examples."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Reduce Motion","type":"heading","anchor":"Reduce-Motion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Loading placeholder’s ring spins via a repeating rotation animation — purely decorative, and exactly the kind of large, continuous motion Reduce Motion exists to suppress. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},{"type":"text","text":" reads SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityReduceMotion"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView"},{"type":"text","text":" reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isReduceMotionEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":" and also observes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.reduceMotionStatusDidChangeNotification"},{"type":"text","text":", so an already-visible spinner responds immediately if the setting changes while on screen, not just on the next appearance. Either way, the ring stays static — still colorful, just not spinning — instead of disabling itself entirely, since a static ring still communicates “loading” on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Increase Contrast","type":"heading","anchor":"Increase-Contrast","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three default placeholders’ gradient icons\/ring respect Increase Contrast — SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorSchemeContrast"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value, UIKit’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isDarkerSystemColorsEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":" (observed live the same way Reduce Motion is). A multi-stop gradient can dip below an acceptable contrast ratio in places a single flat color never does, so when Increase Contrast is on, every gradient is swapped for a solid "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".label"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".primary"},{"type":"text","text":" tint instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Dynamic Type","type":"heading","anchor":"Dynamic-Type","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Error placeholders’ text scales with Dynamic Type: SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" get this for free from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContentUnavailableView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own text styles, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorUIView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s labels use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIFont.preferredFont(forTextStyle: .body, compatibleWith:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Both are covered up to the largest accessibility size by snapshot tests, so a regression that silently pins the text to a fixed size would be caught. The default Loading placeholder has no text at all — its ring is a fixed-size shape, unaffected by Dynamic Type by design."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Identifiers for XCUITest","type":"heading","anchor":"Identifiers-for-XCUITest","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every default placeholder exposes a stable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityIdentifier"},{"type":"text","text":", independent of any localized or custom text, so a UI test can assert which state is showing without string-matching:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identifier"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shown on"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.loading"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.empty"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error.retryButton"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Retry button, when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" is given"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error.secondaryActionButton"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The secondary action button, when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"secondaryAction"},{"type":"text","text":" is given"}]}]]],"header":"row"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Accessibility"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","url":"\/documentation\/sc